ng  that's required for this particular role  now a special tip understand that for  most people it only takes him a few  seconds to apply for a job so for me I  had a big giant ugly paragraph because I  am NOT detail-oriented and I need  someone who would pay attention to  details and within that big ugly giant  paragraph I buried a hidden aquestion so  if the applicant did not answer the  question they were immediately rejected  because why bother reading power letters  and resumes when they didn't even bother  reading your ad okay so we're getting a  much closer we're doing a really good  job in qualifying the applicants and now  you only have the people who really care  about your mission and again if you  stick to the end of this video I will be  sharing with you my actual ad that I  used to hire my assistant step number  five create the page while job ad  reading resumes and cover letters as a  giant a waste of time because it doesn't  actually test people for the skills that  is required for the role the best way to  do it is to partner up and work on a  small project together now Evan has gone  through this process many times over and  in his experience there's always one  person who rises to the top and that is  your guy or girl for this job now this  might be the end of the process for you  and you've already found the right  person for the role however I took it  one step further and I want to share  with you a bonus step in having the  applicants try your product or service  so for me my clients are extremely  to me and anybody who's gonna work for  me they need to know firsthand what my  clients go through so I was down to the  final two applicants and I walked them  through a coaching session with me so  for you you need to decide is it  actually important for your applicants  to try your product or service isn't  even a possibility  but I wanted to give you the option  either way and I have a special shadow  for Tracy folder Tracy thank you so much  f